Comparison: journalctl vs Traditional Logging

Aspect          journalctl             Traditional /var/log/
Storage       Binary format             Plain text 
Performance   Fast indexing             Slower parsing 
Search       Built-in filters          `grep` required 
Metadata     Rich fields (PID, UID, etc.)    Limited 
Rotation      Automatic                  Manual/cron
Forwarding  Built-in (syslog, network)   separate tools 
Security    Forward-secure signatures     Plain text 
Backup       Binary export                 Simple copy 

